479	  <section class="rail-section">
480	    <div class="rail"><span class="rail-num">03</span><span class="rail-label">Insertions</span></div>
481	    <div class="content">
482	      <h2>Three insertions</h2>
483	      <p class="lede">Language-agnostic — the mechanism differs per stack, the question doesn't.</p>
484	      <div class="mechanisms">
485	        <div class="mech">
486	          <div class="mech-num">01</div>
487	          <h3>Interface-completeness check</h3>
488	          <p>When a task touches one implementer of a shared trait / interface / protocol, the plan must cover every other implementer, or state explicitly why not.</p>
489	          <div class="where"><b>Lives in:</b> vector:challenger, dimension 8 — run as a deterministic pre-scan (grep/AST, TDAD-style dependency graph), not an LLM asked to "remember" siblings. Plain tool call; only its structured output enters the agent's context.</div>
490	        </div>
491	        <div class="mech">
492	          <div class="mech-num">02</div>
493	          <h3>Boundary round-trip check</h3>
494	          <p>When a criterion introduces a field on a type another spec persists, serializes, or transmits, that far-side spec needs a matching round-trip criterion — or the gap is named on purpose.</p>
495	          <div class="where"><b>Lives in:</b> canon:audit-spec, as a sixth audit dimension alongside its current five.</div>
496	        </div>
497	        <div class="mech">
498	          <div class="mech-num">03</div>
499	          <h3>Unrepresentable-by-construction</h3>
500	          <p>A value that's sometimes absent, sometimes wrong, or sometimes stale should be a sum type / discriminated union / <code>Result</code> by default — not a bool sitting next to a number. Applies equally to a Rust enum, a TS discriminated union, or a sealed class elsewhere.</p>
501	          <div class="where"><b>Lives in:</b> lambda:implementer's default posture for boundary-crossing fields — reach for this before canon:architect is escalated to, not after.</div>
502	        </div>
503	      </div>
504	    </div>
505	  </section>
