243	        <h1 class="title">The Coding Agent <span>Landscape</span></h1>
244	        <p class="dek">Claude Code, AGY, Codex, opencode, OpenRouter, Augment Code — and whether routing Claude Code through Kimi, GLM, or Qwen is actually worth it.</p>
245	        <div class="verdict">
246	          <span class="verdict-tag">Verdict</span>
247	          <p class="verdict-headline">Keep Claude Code as the primary harness. Tier the models under it — don't switch harnesses.</p>
248	          <ul>
249	            <li><b>No replacement found</b> for this repo's depth of plugin/skill/subagent work — opencode now out-stars Claude Code and leads on heterogeneous teams, but that's a different job.</li>
250	            <li><b>Alt-model routing works, with a catch</b> — Kimi/GLM/Qwen under Claude Code is officially supported and 5–15× cheaper, but breaks native orchestration.</li>
251	            <li><b>The UI is shifting</b> — agents are becoming addressable objects (threads, panes, worktrees), not one chat transcript.</li>
252	            <li class="flag"><b>Live risk</b> — plugin marketplaces have a real malicious-skill problem, and <code>Auto</code> is now the default permission mode.</li>
253	            <li class="flag"><b>Consolidating fast</b> — SpaceX now owns Cursor, Stripe is buying OpenRouter for $7B+, Cognition folded Windsurf into Devin.</li>
254	          </ul>
255	        </div>
