259	    <section id="s1" class="stop">
260	      <div class="stop-head"><span class="stop-num">01</span><div><span class="stop-sub">Anthropic</span><h2>Claude Code: assistant → platform</h2></div></div>
261	      <p class="lede">Near-daily releases (v2.1.211 → v2.1.241 in five weeks). Shape has shifted from "chat with your codebase" to an orchestration layer with its own supply chain and permission model.</p>
262	
263	      <h3 class="label">Plugins &amp; skills</h3>
264	      <ul class="stack">
265	        <li>Marketplace: ZIP/archive sources with SHA-256 pinning, GitLab support, <code>headersHelper</code> short-lived auth, enterprise <code>blockedMarketplaces</code>. Plugins activate without a reload.</li>
266	        <li>Skills hardened: synced skills can no longer shadow local commands or run shell/file expansion from their body.</li>
267	      </ul>
268	      <div class="callout risk">
269	        <p class="callout-title">⚠ Live risk — marketplace supply chain <span class="tag likely">likely</span></p>
270	        <ul>
271	          <li>Documented malicious skills in 2026: dependency hijacking, embedded prompt injection, a Feb. campaign via a marketplace called ClawHub (30+ skills). Snyk sampling: ~36% of scanned skills had security flaws.</li>
272	          <li><b>Do:</b> keep this repo's plugins on a marketplace you control; vet any third-party marketplace before adding it.</li>
273	        </ul>
274	      </div>
275	
276	      <h3 class="label">Three orchestration layers — don't conflate them</h3>
277	      <div class="table-wrap">
278	        <table>
279	          <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>What</th><th>Cost</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
280	          <tbody>
281	            <tr><td class="model-name">Subagents</td><td>Spawn in-session, return a summary</td><td>Low</td><td>Default (nesting depth 3, forking on)</td></tr>
282	            <tr><td class="model-name">Workflows</td><td>Scripted fan-out / pipeline (used for this report)</td><td>Medium</td><td>Default, ~15-agent cap</td></tr>
283	            <tr><td class="model-name">Agent Teams</td><td>Independent teammates message each other, share a task list</td><td>High</td><td>Experimental, opt-in, 3–5 teammates recommended</td></tr>
284	          </tbody>
285	        </table>
286	      </div>
287	
288	      <div class="callout watch">
289	        <p class="callout-title">⚠ Watch — Auto is now the default <span class="tag likely">likely</span></p>
290	        <ul>
291	          <li><code>Auto</code> permission mode replaced ask-per-action CLI-wide on Aug 14.</li>
292	          <li>HN repeatedly cites a March 2026 incident: Claude Code allegedly replaced a Terraform state file and ran <code>terraform destroy</code>, deleting a production RDS database.</li>
293	          <li><b>Do:</b> set sandbox/permission scope explicitly for anything touching infra or credentials — don't rely on the new default.</li>
294	        </ul>
295	      </div>
296	
297	      <h3 class="label">Models &amp; surfaces</h3>
298	      <div class="grid cols-2">
299	        <ul class="stack tight">
300	          <li><b>Opus 5</b> — default Max/Opus model (Jul 24)</li>
301	          <li><b>Sonnet 5</b> — mid-tier, wrote this report</li>
302	          <li><b>Fable 5</b> — days-long autonomous work</li>
303	          <li><b>Fast mode</b> — 2.5× speed at ~2× price (was 6×), free on Max</li>
304	        </ul>
305	        <ul class="stack tight">
306	          <li>Flicker-free terminal renderer</li>
307	          <li>VS Code "Focus View" — collapses tool noise</li>
308	          <li>Expanded JetBrains plugin</li>
309	          <li>Desktop app: sandboxed in-app browser</li>
310	        </ul>
311	      </div>
